WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.024
New single stock ETFs on the TSX give Canadian investors precise alphabet exposure inside their TFSA without direct share ownership. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 201. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:28.024 --> 00:00:37.544
S&amp;P 500 finished at 7,719, down 1.1% on a session that punished risk appetite. NASDAQ

00:00:37.544 --> 00:00:46.904
composite closed at 26,693, down 1.9%, and that index is still up 14.88% year-to-date

00:00:46.904 --> 00:00:57.504
and 19.30% since this shows inception. TSX composite slid 1.1% to 35,584, with banks and

00:00:57.504 --> 00:01:01.064
gold miners leading the drop while growth names took the rotation hit.

00:01:01.544 --> 00:01:08.124
September Core Consumer Price Index, or CPI, printed plus 0.33% month over month,

00:01:08.664 --> 00:01:14.464
and 2.6% year over year, and the beige book added tariff and energy uncertainty on top

00:01:14.464 --> 00:01:15.524
of that firm print.

00:01:16.064 --> 00:01:21.784
The Federal Reserve meeting on October 27th and 28th now carries higher stakes, with markets

00:01:21.784 --> 00:01:26.824
pricing limited room for near-term cuts, and the nearest bank of Canada decision still

00:01:26.824 --> 00:01:30.084
sits weeks out as rate-sensitive sectors reprice the path.

00:01:30.784 --> 00:01:36.604
About 14 days ago, we simulated BTE on a valuation screen that favored resilient cash flow

00:01:36.604 --> 00:01:42.904
through commodity swings, and it closed plus 2.03% when volume actually supported the entry.

00:01:43.797 --> 00:01:50.697
Powerstock listed six single-stock exchange traded funds, or ETFs, on the TSX, Calcine Media

00:01:50.697 --> 00:01:53.957
Reports, and Goop is the share class that tracks Alphabet.

00:01:53.957 --> 00:02:07.717
You implement this the same way you would any concentrated sleeve, open the quote on your platform, read the premium or discount to net asset value or NAV, and size the order so it does not blow through the sector cap you already set.

00:02:08.297 --> 00:02:15.537
These wrappers have historically done their best work in low volatility stretches when a single name can trend without getting whipped around.

00:02:16.097 --> 00:02:22.337
They also amplify draw downs the moment the underlying stock rotates, which is the trade off you accept for precision.

00:02:22.337 --> 00:02:26.777
region. Stack the management fee and the bid ask against two alternatives before you

00:02:26.777 --> 00:02:31.577
click buy, owning the stock itself or a broad sector fund that already holds it.

00:02:32.057 --> 00:02:37.317
For a US name, the structure also folds for an exchange handling into the product, so

00:02:37.317 --> 00:02:41.997
you are not converting currency on every ad or trim. That lets you keep high conviction

00:02:41.997 --> 00:02:47.657
weights inside a registered retirement savings plan, or RRSP, without juggling a separate

00:02:47.657 --> 00:02:53.457
USD cash balance on each ticket. Watch liquidity and tracking error in the opening weeks because

00:02:53.457 --> 00:02:58.217
a new listing can drift from the stock it is supposed to follow until enough volume builds.

00:02:58.737 --> 00:03:04.317
If the discount to NAV is wide, you are paying attacks on impatience. If the spread is wide,

00:03:04.557 --> 00:03:10.674
you are paying attacks on size. Enbridge, ticker ENB, is today's simulated weekly hold.

00:03:11.094 --> 00:03:17.794
A five-session income setup, not a live order and not advice. The Motley Fool Canada flags a 5.8

00:03:17.794 --> 00:03:22.874
80% yield sitting on regulated and take or pay contracts that buffer cash flow when

00:03:22.874 --> 00:03:23.894
commodity swing.

00:03:24.774 --> 00:03:29.334
Technicals on the daily chart show price near the 200-day moving average, support at

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:34.534
recent lows and volume running below the 20-day average, so this is not a volume confirmation

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:35.074
entry.

00:03:35.654 --> 00:03:40.614
Yesterday's catalyst name failed that volume test in a sector already rotating, and that

00:03:40.614 --> 00:03:44.914
is exactly why this pick is a dividend screen rather than another headline-driven growth

00:03:44.914 --> 00:03:45.294
ticket.

00:03:45.294 --> 00:03:52.354
it. Stop sits 8% below entry, which caps a $1,000 simulated position at roughly $80 if

00:03:52.354 --> 00:03:59.154
the thesis breaks. Target is a 2-4% bounce over 5 sessions if yield buyer step in. Anything

00:03:59.154 --> 00:04:04.814
beyond that is luck, not the plan. Confidence is medium, the dividend history and the cash

00:04:04.814 --> 00:04:10.834
flow visibility line up, but sector rotation is still an open risk. Invalidation is explicit,

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:15.474
it, and you should copy this habit on every income name you research. Quarterly results

00:04:15.474 --> 00:04:21.674
that push the distributable cash flow or DCF payout ratio above 75% or an announced

00:04:21.674 --> 00:04:28.562
distribution cut. The screen that matters is the 60-70% DCF payout band, not the headline

00:04:28.562 --> 00:04:32.182
yield, which is how weaker names trap people who only sort on coupon.

00:04:33.022 --> 00:04:37.302
Enbridge has paid dividends for over seven decades and raised the annual payout every

00:04:37.302 --> 00:04:43.322
years since 1995, with a base split across liquid pipelines, natural gas infrastructure,

00:04:43.902 --> 00:04:48.802
gas distribution utilities, and renewable energy, so no single segment has to carry the check.

00:04:49.663 --> 00:04:54.983
We will mark the next open as entry, hold for five sessions unless the stop hits, and

00:04:54.983 --> 00:04:59.863
grade it against the NASDAQ over that same window, a gain that lags the index still counts

00:04:59.863 --> 00:05:00.823
as lost alpha.

00:05:01.423 --> 00:05:07.403
Broadcom, ticker AVGO, was the simulated catalyst hold on announced financing for open AI

00:05:07.403 --> 00:05:14.923
custom AI chip work, and it did not work. Entry was $370 USD and 62 cents at Thursday's

00:05:14.923 --> 00:05:25.063
open. Exit was $346 USD and 25 cents at Wednesday's close. That is a 6.58% loss, or $65.75

00:05:25.063 --> 00:05:27.603
on the $1,000 simulated ticket.

00:05:28.143 --> 00:05:33.623
The financing news never overcame the broader tech rotation once volume lagged, so the catalyst

00:05:33.623 --> 00:05:35.783
Wireless was real and the tape still said no.

00:05:36.323 --> 00:05:40.923
Nasdaq fell less than the position over that matched window, which means the trade produced

00:05:40.923 --> 00:05:43.643
negative alpha even before you look at the dollar loss.

00:05:44.263 --> 00:05:48.663
I would not reuse a catalyst entry next time unless the name is already printing volume

00:05:48.663 --> 00:05:50.063
above its 20-day average.

00:05:50.663 --> 00:05:50.983
Rule.

00:05:51.563 --> 00:05:56.663
Require volume above the 20-day average before entering any catalyst-driven name already in

00:05:56.663 --> 00:05:57.623
a sector rotation.

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:05.980
BlackRock Canada listed the iShares AI Innovation and Tech ETF, ticker XBAI as its first fundamental

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:12.420
active equity ETF, again per CalCine media, with a stock selection mandate rather than a passive

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:19.840
index clone. The fund is TSX listed so it slots into a TFSA or RRSP without the US withholding

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:25.400
tax drag that hits many cross-border dividends. Active management here is cheaper than a typical

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:30.680
mutual fund, which is the buyer this product is built for, an intermediate investor who

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.740
wants a manager, not a closet index.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:38.300
The mandate lets the team shift weight as sub-themed move, including from chip designers

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:42.180
toward power infrastructure names when data-centered demand pulls on the grid.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:47.080
Pull active share and turnover versus passive AI peers before you pay up.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:51.280
If those stats look like the index, the extra fee is not earning its keep.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:56.360
I have no financial relationship with BlackRock or with any brokerage I mentioned later.

00:06:57.359 --> 00:07:05.359
TSMC reported third quarter net profit up 68.7% year over year, hitting 763.1 billion

00:07:05.359 --> 00:07:13.419
new Taiwan dollars, with an operating margin of 58.7% and free cash flow of 476.56 billion.

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:18.779
That print keeps the AI demand story intact for supply chain names that already sit in

00:07:18.779 --> 00:07:20.019
a lot of Canadian accounts.

00:07:20.019 --> 00:07:25.330
The Trump administration is weighing an easing of sanctions on shadow-fleet vessels that

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:30.330
move Russian, Iranian, and Venezuelan oil, a step aimed at pulling global freight

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:30.970
rates down.

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:36.330
Energy infrastructure margins could compress if that supply shows up faster than demand.

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:43.250
Brazil's Senate voted 75-1 to shorten the work week to 40 hours, ending the 6-by-1 schedule

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.090
for roughly 16 million workers with no pay cut.

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:51.050
Yet, multinationals with Brazilian operations will have to bake higher labor costs into

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:51.950
margin forecasts.

00:07:53.056 --> 00:07:57.996
Central Asia Metals' purchase of Cygnus Metals is now effective, the Financial Post

00:07:57.996 --> 00:08:01.476
Reports, which starts the final steps of the scheme of arrangement.

00:08:02.116 --> 00:08:06.856
If you hold the TSXV listing, confirm your election instructions with your broker so you

00:08:06.856 --> 00:08:08.856
are not defaulted into the wrong option.

00:08:09.356 --> 00:08:16.436
The simulated book shows 79 trades at a 51% win rate, an accumulative loss of $95.60

00:08:16.436 --> 00:08:25.216
$0.17 on $1,000 per ticket, with an average return of negative 0.12%, a best of plus 20.11%,

00:08:25.216 --> 00:08:29.136
and a worst of negative 27.14%.

00:08:29.136 --> 00:08:34.656
The rules-based record that a listener can actually reproduce starts August 18, 2026,

00:08:35.296 --> 00:08:41.176
fixed five session holds, entry at the next open, stop or horizon exits, no discretionary

00:08:41.176 --> 00:08:48.156
cuts, and the matched window alpha versus NASDAQ is negative 49.35% across 28 rules-based

00:08:48.156 --> 00:08:53.236
trades. Earlier tickets stay in the archive as history, but they were closed on whatever

00:08:53.236 --> 00:08:58.016
day the run happened to price, so they cannot answer whether this method beats the index.

00:08:59.063 --> 00:09:04.323
The model is adjusting for a pattern we keep paying for. Catalyst names already in rotation,

00:09:04.663 --> 00:09:10.143
entered on light volume. You want 100 shares of a TSX listed energy name at the open,

00:09:10.143 --> 00:09:14.163
and that is where brokerage choice stops being a brand preference and starts

00:09:14.163 --> 00:09:19.003
being a spread problem. Well simple trade charges no commission yet it routes

00:09:19.003 --> 00:09:22.743
through a single market maker that can widen the spread by three to five cents

00:09:22.743 --> 00:09:27.743
on less liquid names in the first 15 minutes. Quest trade charges four dollars and

00:09:27.743 --> 00:09:33.443
95 cents to nine dollars and 95 cents per ticket with free ETF buys and direct

00:09:33.443 --> 00:09:38.923
US exchange access plus real-time level two data on the higher tier. Interactive

00:09:38.923 --> 00:09:46.483
broker's post margin around 6.5% for balances under $100,000 and reaches 150 plus global

00:09:46.483 --> 00:09:52.423
markets at the cost of a steeper interface. Bank desks such as TD Direct Investing sit

00:09:52.423 --> 00:09:59.083
neatly beside your checking account and then levy $9.99 a trade plus fatter foreign exchange

00:09:59.083 --> 00:10:05.383
spreads on US names. Run aside-by-side cost calculator for your actual size and frequency before

00:10:05.383 --> 00:10:06.883
or you commit a registered account.

00:10:07.443 --> 00:10:10.343
Then send the larger US orders to the lowest fee desk.

00:10:10.863 --> 00:10:13.283
The misconception is that free is always cheapest.

00:10:13.963 --> 00:10:15.663
Hidden spreads and missing order types

00:10:15.663 --> 00:10:17.183
can cost an active investor

00:10:17.183 --> 00:10:18.603
more than a posted commission.

00:10:19.243 --> 00:10:23.703
Confirm automatic dividend reinvestment inside the TFSA or RSP

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:27.003
because a missing DRIP forces manual buys

00:10:27.003 --> 00:10:29.003
that reintroduce commissions and FX.

00:10:29.763 --> 00:10:31.923
On a $50,000 borrowed balance,

00:10:32.223 --> 00:10:34.763
the interactive broker's rate can save hundreds of dollars

00:10:34.763 --> 00:10:39.843
a year versus a bank platform, only if you are willing to learn its order types and reporting.

00:10:40.443 --> 00:10:45.843
I have no financial relationship with well-simple, quest trade, interactive brokers, or the bank-owned

00:10:45.843 --> 00:10:53.622
desks. Open your brokerage app, pull the QQQ holdings breakdown, and line up your NVDA, AAPL,

00:10:53.802 --> 00:10:58.902
and MSFT weights against those percentages. Trim any single name that sits more than three

00:10:58.902 --> 00:11:04.342
percentage points above your own cap. Before we wrap, tomorrow I will apply the new volume rule

00:11:04.342 --> 00:11:09.322
to whatever catalyst tape shows up, and I will not simulate an entry if the 20-day average

00:11:09.322 --> 00:11:14.522
is not there. That's modern investing techniques for today. If you found this useful, share

